Serialised: Wine's console is a single per-prefix server, so concurrent clients
attaching to it interfere. The failure signature is unmistakable and is NOT ours —
the ORACLE produces no output at all while ARET produces its own. Each of these
passes alone.

The whole console family is marked at once rather than one fixture per observed
flap: the cause is shared, and adding markers as they flap costs a full parallel run
to discover each one while leaving the gate randomly red in between.
